From: Tanmay Shah <tanmay.shah@amd.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 17:48:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: core: Full attach detach during recovery
References: bsc#1258210
Patch-mainline: 6.18.61
Git-commit: d93ffd549fb4df18c934ca7a47d4128a18c718cb

[ Upstream commit d93ffd549fb4df18c934ca7a47d4128a18c718cb ]

Current attach on recovery mechanism loads the clean resource table
during recovery, but doesn't re-allocate the resources. RPMsg
communication will fail after recovery due to this. Fix this
incorrect behavior by doing the full detach and attach of remote
processor during the recovery. This will load the clean resource table
and re-allocate all the resources, which will set up correct vring
information in the resource table.

Signed-off-by: Tanmay Shah <tanmay.shah@amd.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260630004806.3835488-2-tanmay.shah@amd.com
Signed-off-by: Mathieu Poirier <mathieu.poirier@linaro.org>
Signed-off-by: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Robert Frohl <rfrohl@suse.com>
---
 drivers/remoteproc/remoteproc_core.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/remoteproc_core.c b/drivers/remoteproc/remoteproc_core.c
index bbc781e41a1b..2336c55eb021 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/remoteproc_core.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/remoteproc_core.c
@@ -1784,7 +1784,20 @@ static int rproc_attach_recovery(struct rproc *rproc)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	return __rproc_attach(rproc);
+	/* clean up all acquired resources */
+	rproc_resource_cleanup(rproc);
+
+	/* release HW resources if needed */
+	rproc_unprepare_device(rproc);
+
+	rproc_disable_iommu(rproc);
+
+	/* Free the copy of the resource table */
+	kfree(rproc->cached_table);
+	rproc->cached_table = NULL;
+	rproc->table_ptr = NULL;
+
+	return rproc_attach(rproc);
 }
 
 static int rproc_boot_recovery(struct rproc *rproc)
-- 
